00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
May the schwartz be with you.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Spaceballs is a comedy, science fiction film directed by Mel Brooks.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
When the nefarious Dark Helmet hatches a plan to snatch Princess Vespa and steal her planet's
air, space-bum-for-hire Lone Starr and his clueless sidekick fly to the rescue.

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Along the way, they meet Yogurt, who puts Lone Starr wise to the power of
"The Schwartz." Can he master it in time to save the day?

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
President Skroob / Yogurt, played by Mel Brooks.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Barf, played by John Candy.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Dark Helmet, played by Rick Moranis.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Lone Starr, played by Bill Pullman.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Princess Vespa, played by Daphne Zuniga.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
King Roland, played by Dick Van Patten.

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Spaceballs 2 is an upcoming American space opera parody
film and the sequel to Spaceballs (1987).

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
It is directed by Josh Greenbaum and written by Josh
Gad, Benji Samit and Dan Hernandez.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film sees Mel Brooks, Rick Moranis (in his first live-action film role in 30 years), Bill Pullman, George Wyner, and Daphne Zuniga
reprising their roles from the previous film, while Gad, Keke Palmer, Lewis Pullman and Anthony Carrigan join the cast.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
Like its predecessor, the film will primarily be a parody of Star
Wars, but will also parody other popular media.

15
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It is scheduled for a release in 2027.

16
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
The film explores themes of galaxy, android, space marine, laser gun, temple.

17
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and thought_provoking.
